{"q":"349","t":"Intersection of Two Arrays","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given two integer arrays <code>nums1</code> and <code>nums2</code>, return <em>an array of their <span data-keyword=\"array-intersection\">intersection</span></em>. Each element in the result must be <strong>unique</strong> and you may return the result in <strong>any order</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums1 = [1,2,2,1], nums2 = [2,2]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [2]\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums1 = [4,9,5], nums2 = [9,4,9,8,4]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [9,4]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> [4,9] is also accepted.\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums1.length, nums2.length &lt;= 1000</code></li>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= nums1[i], nums2[i] &lt;= 1000</code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"intersection\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"nums1\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"nums2\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Hash Table","slug":"hash-table"},{"name":"Two Pointers","slug":"two-pointers"},{"name":"Binary Search","slug":"binary-search"},{"name":"Sorting","slug":"sorting"}],"s":[{"t":"Intersection of Two Arrays II","s":"intersection-of-two-arrays-ii","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Intersection of Three Sorted Arrays","s":"intersection-of-three-sorted-arrays","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Find the Difference of Two Arrays","s":"find-the-difference-of-two-arrays","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Count Common Words With One Occurrence","s":"count-common-words-with-one-occurrence","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Choose Numbers From Two Arrays in Range","s":"choose-numbers-from-two-arrays-in-range","d":"Ha